From: "ELEVARIQ Agent (Claude)" <connectroman3@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:20:15 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(security): V2.1 Phase B/E Rule K matrix false
 negatives; unrecognized remote operations

Phase B (Rule K, 120-case expected-vs-actual matrix): a command-only K rule closes
14 false negatives (interpreter/nested-shell environment dumps, /proc/*/environ,
[Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariables, gh auth token, npm auth config, macOS
keychain, keymgr, Windows Credentials/Protect). Not applied to Write/Edit content,
so source that passes process.env to a child process may still be written.
Matrix with the providers' protected list: 0 FN, 4 accepted conservative FP.
69-probe suite unchanged: 0 V2.1 bypasses, 0 legitimate regressions.

Phase E: gh pr merge / repo sync / repo delete / repo edit / release delete,
gh secret|variable set, npm unpublish / deprecate / dist-tag now need approval.
Tests characterize approval semantics through the runner, including the documented
gaps (approvals never expire; a category, not a command, is approved).
